# VideoBrief — Stack

## Core

- Next.js (App Router) + React + TypeScript — use `src/` layout
- pnpm + Vercel
- Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui + lucide-react
- React Hook Form + Zod
- TanStack Query (client mutations / analysis-state polling; RSC for primary reads)
- next-themes — **dark mode default** (respect system after first choice)
- next-intl — **English only** for MVP (scaffold for later locales)

## Data & auth

- Supabase Auth: email/password + Google OAuth + **anonymous guests** (personal GCP project)
- Guest → permanent via `updateUser` / `linkIdentity` (same `user.id`); soft email confirmation
- Drizzle ORM + Drizzle Kit migrations on Supabase Postgres
- `@supabase/ssr` for session/cookies; never trust client-supplied `user_id`
- RLS on all user-owned tables

## AI & YouTube

- Vercel AI SDK behind an `AIProvider` abstraction
- Default model: `analysisConfig` (OpenRouter). Zod-validate all structured LLM output before persist
- Transcript/metadata: `youtubei.js` behind a swappable `TranscriptProvider`
- Player: `react-youtube` (IFrame API — seek/time sync required)
- English captions only; if missing → clear error (no Whisper)

## Billing

- Stripe Billing: Checkout (`mode: subscription`) + Customer Portal
- Webhooks update `profiles.plan` (source of truth for entitlement)
- Stripe SDK only behind `src/lib/stripe` + `src/domain/billing`
- Env: `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`, `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`, `STRIPE_PRICE_PRO_MONTHLY`

## Explicitly not used

Prisma, tRPC, PostHog, Jest (use Vitest), Playwright (post-MVP)

Redis + BullMQ are used for the **analysis queue, per-video lock, and monthly usage counters**. Do not cache transcripts or classification in Redis.

## Commands

```bash
pnpm dev | worker | build | start | lint | format | test | type-check
pnpm drizzle-kit generate | migrate | studio
```

